    "body": "Default update after manual testing:\n\nA Linear lead runs parallel to the selected edge. On this part, that tangent direction starts the plunge inside the finished surface. The full-cone check correctly refuses it. A Perpendicular lead starts on the physical air side and works on this edge selection.\n\nNew 2D Chamfer operations now default to Perpendicular, 3 mm, with the same lead for lead-out. Legacy saved projects keep their old compatibility behavior. Users can still select None or another lead shape.\n\nNew head: `4188f677ffbc5280c6ddda785c81f292cca11dd1`.\n\nFocused verification:\n- App Chamfer lead tests: 3 passed.\n- MCP Chamfer lead tests: 1 passed.\n- UI Chamfer lead tests: 3 passed.\n- Clippy for app and UI: passed.\n\nThis push changes the head and waits for a fresh review.\r\n",
